    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0355" n="343" xml:id="pg343"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/13203½: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-16T12:00:00+02:00">July 16,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received July 16—7:19 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3012. For the President and the Acting Secretary. Delivered your 2600, July 14th,
                    to the Prime Minister personally. I know he feels as you do on this subject. At
                    the same time he is asking Mr. Eden<anchor n="3" xml:id="d364-f1"/> to get a
                    complete statement covering all situations which will be forwarded to you. He
                    was delighted to hear that Harry is coming. So am I.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d364-f1" n="3" xml:id="d364-f1-content">
                <p>Anthony Eden, British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
